{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-21T16:53:34.594Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d9cc3776c9633656a5e1057","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-21T16:53:34.594Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-21T16:53:34.594Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Pre-change diagnosis: PR #94 uses one logistic weight times a strictly positive log-title-length feature. Its greedy classifier is necessarily constant, so more samples, higher learning rate or more updates cannot make it useful. The held-out set has 36 closed and 5 other items, so always-closed scores 36/41=0.8780487805; the stochastic reward correctly penalizes uncertainty and cannot be substituted with greedy accuracy. Eight updates and 256 samples learn the majority slowly (0.5980 then 0.6810), but capacity is the primary defect. Holding every identical projected length in one partition is conservative yet prevents renamed-input leakage; retain this exact split. Proposed bounded intercept plus hashed title-word vector has no status/ID features and keeps all title-identical inputs together. Add deterministic paired bootstrap confidence intervals over held-out items against BOTH constant actions and the incumbent, in addition to existing sampled, exact-improvement and gap gates. Increase only explicit approved fit/sample allowances; retain every failed frontier and never relax the gate. Existing prefix/rsipower items cover broader chronological forecasting and transfer, distinct from this snapshot-recognition child."}]}],"before_hash":"ee2fd15fa65f66768379ed78282e01c3afc3be40d6b9e6f86ba4080ab7764a73","after_hash":"3d389c2d6fa5d639bc8b95840a39e9173c3afc2e721127245237474a2e2aec6b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d641b4fb9b042ba89d5e402de75e7496cb932464e2d1baca45d94f2726feb513"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-21T17:00:36.486Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d9cc3776c9633656a5e1057","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-21T17:00:36.485Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Implementation in progress: bounded 64-column title-only features plus an intercept, unchanged source-action importance weighting, versioned vector checkpoint digests and full resume verification. Item-paired percentile bootstrap uses 8192 deterministic resamples, 41 held-out items rather than 40000 repeated rollouts, and Bonferroni-adjusted intervals for incumbent and both constant actions. Existing sampled confidence/effect, exact improvement and gap gates remain additional requirements. A preliminary numerical probe still trails the constant baseline; no win is claimed. Explicit sealed retry_rejected exploration will attempt three generations while keeping refused checkpoints out of collection and preserving all per-job reservations. Legacy scalar programmes keep their exact identities and stop semantics."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-21T17:00:36.486Z"}],"before_hash":"3d389c2d6fa5d639bc8b95840a39e9173c3afc2e721127245237474a2e2aec6b","after_hash":"a597374b20d735cc8ae010d0689e2516c7b0e36e8038e0772156288ec2bb5694","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash"