{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-21T17:11:46.624Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d9cc3776c9633656a5e1057","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-21T17:11:46.623Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Three real external attempts on the same public pm-ops commit and original split are complete: n_train=105, n_held_out=41, baseline=36/41=0.8780487805. Held-out expected rewards and nominal 95% item-bootstrap CIs: g1 0.8713980699 [0.7743570291,0.9668509885], g2 0.8645003749 [0.7683455624,0.9579166612], g3 0.8534392510 [0.7593053408,0.9436312068]. All three are refused against the constant; zero promoted successors. Every collection used the unchanged seed policy; the derived learning rates were 1,0.5,0.25. The baseline still wins and no gate was weakened. Each job charged 256 optimizer updates exactly once; 3072 actions were collected. Resume verified all three, preserved checkpoint bytes, launched no new job, and status agreed. Source inventory bytes are unchanged. Execution used a PATH without Git and a plain controller tracker. Complete metrics, adjusted paired differences and full digests are in docs/baseline-frontier-evidence.json. Diagnostic log-loss fitting was worse (first score 0.7492), so it was not adopted."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-21T17:11:46.624Z"}],"before_hash":"8a874bd03f7980afe68975f9a0311458e22b43b64c48e617a36e4f8cfd3ee57a","after_hash":"f6493d3df5e41b95c937c324610073a74c18d7e522d5a6e1a1280f4465f420a4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"fe68dcca6f97ba4f164b106c5cc8706bda5cb1b8a27e276e421172da8f9d42ae"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-21T17:11:53.431Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"5d9cc3776c9633656a5e1057","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-21T17:11:53.431Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Behavioural revert proof in isolated source copies: removing only the vector fit dispatch makes the three-promotion capacity regression fail (1 failed, exit 1); disabling only application of the item gate makes the improving-but-below-constant regression fail (1 failed, exit 1). Restoring both functions passes the two focused regressions (2/2, zero failures/skips). No production source was modified during the ongoing release gate."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-21T17:11:53.431Z"}],"before_hash":"f6493d3df5e41b95c937c324610073a74c18d7e522d5a6e1a1280f4465f420a4","after_hash":"d7079133779c3e8b8e4fee7eb0319a1081d66cc1c4654ee9aafe58b3e3375c03","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e5b3507dc12cfd9c9b6c6326d184734ff5ddc3e38869bedbc1f829662d530677"}
